<section class="block-section story">
  <span class="section-tag">Story</span>
  <h2>What this page is about</h2>
  <p class="sub">Take-home 2, part 1. The unit's anchor question: <em>How do you build for a planet that occasionally tries to destroy what you've built?</em></p>
  <p>In Take-home 1 you met the four settings. This page goes deeper on the two that account for most coastal-city hazards on Earth: subduction zones (Tōhoku, Cascadia, Sumatra) and transform faults (Anatolian, San Andreas). The same physics produces the same hazards everywhere a boundary type exists. By the end you'll be able to look at any city on a coast and predict, with reasonable confidence, what its dominant hazards are.</p>
</section>

